 the GPL-2.0-only binary: a GPL-2.0-only consumer takes the MIT arm, which
 carries none of the "further restrictions" that GPLv2 section 6 forbids,
 while the Apache-2.0 arm matches upstream PAPPL for anyone reusing the
 bindings elsewhere. See docs/DECISIONS.md, Q-8a.

